= mathed + Slint

A block that starts with `\slint` is not typeset by Typst. Its body — everything
after the marker — is [Slint](https://slint.dev) DSL, compiled and rasterised by
the `mathed_slint_browser` helper process, and shown inline as a live widget.

The widgets below are **interactive**: click one to give it keyboard focus, then
type into it. Click elsewhere in the document to hand focus back.

\slint 480x200
import { VerticalBox, LineEdit, Button } from "std-widgets.slint";

export component Demo inherits Window {
    background: #203040;
    VerticalBox {
        padding: 16px;
        spacing: 10px;
        // `Text` is a Slint builtin, not a std-widget — do not import it.
        Text { text: "rendered by the Slint mini-browser"; color: #e0e8f0; }
        LineEdit { text: "hello slint"; }
        Button { text: "click me"; }
    }
}

The marker may carry a size, `\slint WIDTHxHEIGHT`, as above. It defaults to
480x240 and is clamped to 4096 so a typo cannot ask for a 100000-pixel buffer.
A widget is a normal Slint component, so state survives between frames — this
counter keeps your clicks:

\slint 260x110
import { Button, VerticalBox } from "std-widgets.slint";

export component Counter inherits Window {
    background: #16202c;
    in-out property <int> clicks: 0;
    // Behind everything, so a click anywhere in the widget counts. The button
    // declared after it still wins where the two overlap.
    TouchArea {
        clicked => { root.clicks += 1; }
    }
    VerticalBox {
        padding: 10px;
        spacing: 6px;
        Text {
            text: "clicks: " + root.clicks;
            color: #e0e8f0;
            font-size: 20px;
            horizontal-alignment: center;
        }
        Button {
            text: "increment";
            clicked => { root.clicks += 1; }
        }
    }
}

Everything after a blank line is ordinary Typst again — headings, math and hidden
markers all keep working around a widget:

$ \int_0^1 x^2 \,dx = \tfrac{1}{3} $

The block scanner keeps a `\slint` block whole across the blank lines inside its
component, so the DSL does not need to be written on a single line.
